    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Ii chord",
      "body": "The chord on the 2nd degree is the **ii chord**, a minor chord. In C major it is D minor.\n\n**Why it matters:** The ii often leads to V. It is a softer way to set up the pull back home, used all over jazz and soul.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        62,
        65,
        69
      ],
      "labels": {
        "62": "D (ii)",
        "65": "F",
        "69": "A"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Iii chord",
      "body": "The chord on the 3rd degree is the **iii chord**, also minor. In C major it is E minor.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the least used of the seven, so when a song does use it, it stands out as a fresh colour.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        64,
        67,
        71
